nthe fibre of\n<MATH_0042>\nover <MATH_0043> is homotopy equivalent to a point. In fact we\nwill show this map is a trivial Kan fibration. Namely,\n<MATH_0044> is a trivial can fibration. For any ring <MATH_0045>\nwe have\n<MATHSEG_0001> finite<MATHSEG_0002>\n(filtered colimit). Thus the displayed map of simplicial sets is a\nfiltered colimit of trivial Kan fibrations, whence a trivial Kan fibration\nby Simplicial, Lemma <REF_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6ee41aa2177d2e94ab66c1c35c1602230502d2b1958e028593e66bb362458831", "unit_id": "tag:08QV:proof"}
